IMPORT `ocar-11-12-cover`

-- IMPORTS form one chain (each module imports the one before it), because l4 checks a
-- module again for every path it is imported by. Names are visible down the chain. This
-- module draws on: ocar-nouns, ocar-01-definitions.

-- O-Car rules, Article 13 (how the sum insured and the vehicle's value are determined).
-- Quotations are generated from ../../source/raw/opes-ocar.txt.
--
-- WHAT IS HERE. 13.1 describes how the Insurer finds the market value of a new and of a used
-- vehicle; those are descriptions of a valuation, which the caller supplies as `market value
-- when insured`. 13.2 gives a formula for when the parties cannot determine it, with a table
-- of minimum remaining-quality rates. Its last bullet says that under- and over-insurance are
-- settled on the market value; 14.1.2 applies that.

§ `Article 13 — Determining the sum insured`

§§ `13.1 — insuring at or below market value; how the market value is found`

-- Inert: the Policyholder may insure at or below market value (1.10 says the same; tested
-- there), and the two bullets describe the valuation the caller supplies.
